  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a contributor checking #870, I want a captured, anonymized topic list of one category on the **Favoris** and **Suivis** filters with rows in them, so that the four filters can be compared on real rows instead of empty states.\n\n### Context\n\nPR #1232 renders the four filters from captured fixtures: Tous (`R04-list-cat13-p1-anon`) and Lus (`R08-2-list-cat13-owntopic2`) have rows, but Suivis (`R08-1`) and Favoris (`R08-3`) are captures with no rows, and `R09` (labelled owntopic3) is an anonymous capture that returned the plain list. Nothing may be hand-built (LESSONS 36).\n\n### Scope\n\n- Logged in (operator's test account), one category, the Favoris and the Suivis filter, each holding at least two flagged topics: the list pages as the app requests them (the filter URL the app sends, from `TopicFlagFilterPicker` / the topic list client).\n- Anonymize and check independently (FIXTURES.md, LESSONS 33-34); add them to the MANIFEST. Read-only capture: no write.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Two anonymized captures with rows, in the fixtures, `check --corpus` clean.\n- [ ] #870's hosted test (PR #1232 or its follow-up) uses them, and the light and dark screenshots of the four filters are posted on #870.\n\n### Wanted by\n\n#870\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
